            "      \n",
            "        <div data-see-more-text=\"more\" data-see-more-link=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/moniqueruffbell_ted2026-ideaschangeeverything-vancouver-activity-7449153858087489536-CNS_\" class=\"see-more-text overflow-hidden whitespace-break-spaces\n",
            "            max-h-[64px]\n",
            "            no-underline text-color-text text-sm font-normal px-2\n",
            "            mb-1.5\" style=\"overflow: hidden;\">We have lift off. TED2026 Vancouver starts in less than 24 hours and I am more excited about this year than ever before.\n",
            "\n",
            "I'll be honest...I flew into Vancouver heavy. Exhausted from heartache and worry from everything happening in this world, carrying more than I probably should. But TED reminds you why you do this work. I couldn't wait to get into the TED bubble.\n",
            "\n",
            "Within hours of landing, I was surrounded by familiar faces, new collaborators, and the kind of people who still genuinely believe that change can happen in the very best way. Our theme this year is ALL OF US, and that's exactly what its going to take to move forward in this world. Hope and optimism aren't just themes here. They're truly the main ingredient of why people love this conference. \n",
            "\n",
            "And we are going to send off our community with love and nostalgia from Vancouver with our TED Yearbook! It's a full chapter of TED's history in Vancouver from 2014 to 2026 to close out this week (and yes, you need to get your yearbook signed!). There's just something profound about being present for the end of an era and the beginning of what's next when we make our move to San Diego.\n",
            "\n",
            "If you're in Vancouver this week, come find me. If you're watching from home, stay tuned, the ideas coming off that stage are going to be worth your attention.\n",
